  # NET DIRECTED ASYMMETRY (ANTS 2026 best paper, see header) — a pair whose cross-correlation function
  # is SYMMETRIC about zero lag has no leader, and neither of the older guards can see it: |r| is high
  # (0.72 here, over MIN_R) and the persistence baseline is ~0 (white driver, so Y does not predict its
  # own future), so eff clears MARGIN in BOTH directions and the pre-fix code named whichever direction
  # sampling noise happened to favour. Fixture carries two pairs at once:
