  # wifi pair), yet the two channels' own persistences are far apart (|r_xx| 0.81 vs |r_yy| 0.37).
  # The old net = eff(X->Y) - eff(Y->X) collapses to that persistence gap: +0.41, four times the ASYM
  # floor, and "Smooth movement PREDICTS Jagged movement" shipped to the ideas queue.
  # The gate is on the STATISTIC'S OWN DEFINITION, checked against the numbers the finding publishes:
  # net must BE |fwd r| - |reverse r|. That is red under the old formula for this fixture (it reports
  # +0.41 where the cross difference is -0.02) and green under the new one, and unlike a threshold it
  # cannot be satisfied by tuning a floor. Asserted BOTH ways, like the mutual pair above: with the
  # asymmetry gate OFF the pair IS emitted (so the fixture is a real trap and reaches the gate), and
  # with it on the pair is gone while the genuinely asymmetric Lead1->Lead2 survives.
  pb="$_td/persistence.log"
  # The generator PRINTS the four lag-1 correlations it planted, so the trap can be proven
  # arithmetically instead of by hoping the tool emits it. That matters here: under the FIXED
  # statistic this pair nets ~0 and is dropped by the score floor as well as by ASYM, so "turn the
  # gate off and watch the bad finding appear" — the shape the mutual fixture above uses — is not
  # constructible. What IS constructible is the fact the bug consisted of: OLD net >= ASYM while the
  # cross difference is ~0.
  ptrap="$(python3 - "$pb" <<'PY2'
import sys,math,random,datetime as dt
out=open(sys.argv[1],"w"); base=dt.datetime(2026,6,21,0,0,0,tzinfo=dt.timezone.utc)
N=140
rj=random.Random(11)                                    # jitter that roughens JAGGED only
rd=random.Random(29); D=[rd.randint(-10,10) for _ in range(N+6)]   # the ASYMMETRIC pair's driver
X=[];Y=[]
for i in range(N):
    t=(base+dt.timedelta(seconds=300*i)).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
    W=round(12*math.sin(2*math.pi*i/10))                # ONE driver, reaching both at the SAME instant
    sm=-55+W                                            # sees it clean  -> deltas strongly persistent
    jg=-70+W+rj.randint(-4,4)                           # sees it rough  -> deltas barely persistent
    X.append(sm); Y.append(jg)
    l1=-58+D[i+2]; l2=-62+D[i]                          # a REAL one-way lead, keeps the null alive
    devs=("%d|BB:BB:BB:BB:BB:01|Smooth %d|BB:BB:BB:BB:BB:02|Jagged "
          "%d|BB:BB:BB:BB:BB:03|Lead1 %d|BB:BB:BB:BB:BB:04|Lead2"%(sm,jg,l1,l2))
    out.write("%s host n=4 devices=[%s]\n"%(t,devs))
out.close()
def corr(a,b):
    n=len(a); ma=sum(a)/n; mb=sum(b)/n
    sa=math.sqrt(sum((v-ma)**2 for v in a)); sb=math.sqrt(sum((v-mb)**2 for v in b))
    return sum((u-ma)*(v-mb) for u,v in zip(a,b))/(sa*sb) if sa and sb else 0.0
d=lambda v:[v[i]-v[i-1] for i in range(1,len(v))]
dx,dy=d(X),d(Y)
rxy=corr(dx[:-1],dy[1:]); ryx=corr(dy[:-1],dx[1:])
rxx=corr(dx[:-1],dx[1:]);  ryy=corr(dy[:-1],dy[1:])
old=(abs(rxy)-abs(ryy))-(abs(ryx)-abs(rxx))             # what the pre-2026-08-19 net computed
print("%.3f %.3f %.3f"%(old, abs(rxy)-abs(ryx), abs(rxy)))
PY2
)"
  # THE FIXTURE IS A TRAP, proven in numbers: the old net clears the ASYM floor (0.10) several times
  # over while the cross difference is ~0 and the forward |r| is over MIN_R, i.e. every gate the old
  # code had would have passed this pair through as "Smooth movement PREDICTS Jagged movement".
  set -- $ptrap
  awk -v old="$1" -v cross="$2" -v fwd="$3" 'BEGIN{
      if (old < 0.25)        { print "  FAIL: fixture is not a trap — the OLD net on it is " old ", not comfortably over the 0.10 ASYM floor"; exit 1 }
      if ((cross<0?-cross:cross) > 0.10) { print "  FAIL: fixture is not a trap — its cross terms are asymmetric (" cross "), so a real direction is present and the persistence bias is not isolated"; exit 1 }
      if ((fwd<0?-fwd:fwd) < 0.60)       { print "  FAIL: fixture is not a trap — forward |r| " fwd " is under MIN_R, so the old code would have dropped it before the net mattered"; exit 1 }
    }' || fail=1
  _pcall(){ LEADLAG_PRESENCE="$pb" LEADLAG_WINDOW_H=48 LEADLAG_BIN_S=300 LEADLAG_MIN_OVERLAP=8 \
